// chriz-iwd-encounters 200: an enemy priest prepares the moment it first sees
// the party. Like SCS's precasts, it casts instantly a spell it has memorised
// and spends that copy, so it is ready earlier, not stronger.
//   Self-protection, on the difficulties the install-time setting below names:
//     one from its own spells (Barkskin, else Armor of Faith, else Draw Upon Holy
//     Might); with none of them, a free Armor of Faith, which every priest class
//     can cast.
//   Hard (priest level 7 and up) and Insane (every priest): one group blessing
//     from its own spells (Recitation, else Prayer, else Bless). Chant is left
//     out: in IWD:EE it stops the caster's spellcasting for a turn.
// Each part fires once per creature. Every block ends in Continue(), so the AI
// below this point runs as before.
// Install-time setting for the self-protection blocks: %cie_self_note%

IF
  Global("CIE_SELF","LOCALS",0)
  %cie_self_gate%
  Allegiance(Myself,ENEMY)
  OR(3)
    Class(Myself,CLERIC_ALL)
    Class(Myself,DRUID_ALL)
    Class(Myself,SHAMAN)
  See(NearestEnemyOf(Myself))
  !StateCheck(Myself,STATE_REALLY_DEAD)
  HaveSpell(CLERIC_BARKSKIN)
THEN
  RESPONSE #100
    SetGlobal("CIE_SELF","LOCALS",1)
    ReallyForceSpell(Myself,CLERIC_BARKSKIN)
    RemoveSpell(CLERIC_BARKSKIN)
    Continue()
END

IF
  Global("CIE_SELF","LOCALS",0)
